# "Ward abilities of those creatures don't trigger" stops a trigger, not one that is already on the stack. Bot2's Lightning Bolt
# targets Bot1's Sedgemoor Witch (Ward - Pay 3 life) and the ward ability triggers; Bot2 then flashes in Nowhere to Run in
# response. Its enters trigger kills the Witch (-3/-3), and the ward ability, already on the stack, still resolves: Bot2 is asked
# and pays 3 life (20 to 17). Had the ward been dropped, Bot2 would not have been asked and would still be at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Sedgemoor Witch
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Nowhere to Run
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sedgemoor Witch.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Sedgemoor Witch)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Accept
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Sedgemoor Witch
Bot2.Battlefield.Nowhere to Run.Types = Enchantment
